    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783">

                <pb facs="0728" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg716"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/7–1244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-12T18:00:00-04:00">July 12, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>130. It has been agreed by the Department and the Foreign Office that the
                    American and British Governments send the following instruction <pb facs="0729"
                        n="717" xml:id="pg717"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi> to their respective diplomatic
                    representatives at Jidda, these instructions being repeated to Mr. Landis’
                    office in Cairo by the Department<anchor n="19" xml:id="d783-f1"/> and to Lord
                        Moyne<anchor n="20" xml:id="d783-f2"/> by the Foreign Office: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The joint programme for supply and financial aid towards Saudi Arabia
                            which has been agreed upon by the U.S. Government and His Majesty’s
                            Government in the United Kingdom is to be regarded as the expression of
                            a single combined policy in this field towards Saudi Arabia on the part
                            of the two Governments. In the light of this policy you are to treat all
                            proposals for supply and financial aid to Saudi Arabia jointly with your
                            British colleague. You should cooperate with him closely and
                            wholeheartedly. Any approach to the Saudi Arabia Government in this
                            field should in future be made jointly with him.</p>
                        <p>2. Identical instructions are being sent to your British colleague.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d783-f1" n="19" xml:id="d783-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Cairo as telegram 1781, “for AEMME” (American Economic Mission,
                    Middle East, Cairo headquarters of James M. Landis).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d783-f2" n="20" xml:id="d783-f2-content">
                <p>British Minister Resident in the Middle East.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
